WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our next guest is the host

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:05.004
of "Love About Town,"
available at Apple Podcasts.

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.939
Making her television debut,

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.409
please welcome the very funny
Kenice Mobley.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.678
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:15.881
-Hello. Hello. Hi. Hi.

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:18.084
I see a couple of men here.
A couple.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.554
I do need to warn
all of the men, okay?

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.290
The second all this is over,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.426
I'm making out
with everyone, okay?

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:27.694
Everyone.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.096
I saw a couple
kissing on the street,

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:34.333
and my first thought was,
"Let me get in on that."

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:35.902
They did not like that. Okay.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.737
They don't like it
when you say that to them.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.005
They're against it.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:42.275
I am single right now, okay,
at this moment.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:45.812
But according to rom-com logic,
I did go up to my roof

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.980
and I shouted,
"I don't need a man!"

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.916
and, "I never want
to get married!"

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.951
So he should be coming
at any moment. Okay?

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.753
Do you guys, like,
hear a helicopter?

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.454
I think he's on his way.
I just --

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.189
I feel confident about it.

00:00:57.189 --> 00:00:59.859
Look, truly, I don't know
if I ever want to get married,

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:03.396
but I do know
that I want my death

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:07.100
to ruin a man's life...

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.402
to the point where
he has to do paperwork.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.204
That's important to me. It is.
It's very important to me.

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:14.306
I do see people I date
from time to time.

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:16.976
I told my mom about one
of the guys that I'm seeing,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.278
and she was like,
"Oh, that's nice, Kenice,

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:21.781
but, um, quick question.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.550
Is he...

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.252
or...?"

00:01:27.252 --> 00:01:29.588
Some of you look
a little confused.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:32.024
Yes, this is the white side
of my hand,

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:34.626
this is the black side
of my hand.

00:01:34.626 --> 00:01:36.195
-Woman: Whoo!
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:38.364
Which -- I think it's funny
that, to my mom,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:43.002
there are only
two races of people.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:46.238
What I actually said was,
"Why, yes, Mom!

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:49.208
This time I got one with hands
and everything, so..."

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:51.377
No, me and that guy
pretty seriously

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.646
had the family conversation
where I was talking about

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.414
starting one
and he was letting me know

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:59.752
that he already had a wife and
child, so fun times, fun times.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.655
Completely unrelated question --

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:08.094
where do you guys stand
on dogs with people names?

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.764
Some shrugging.
Some side to side.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.633
I don't know what that means.
Okay, it's a mix.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:16.769
It's a mix. All right.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.673
I am for it, okay?
I am for it.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.842
I am for it because I think

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:27.780
it makes it clear
who is okay with slavery.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.883
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:36.055
No, because if you are willing
to take a living being,

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:39.325
you know, and name it Stephanie
and put it in your basement

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.462
and tell it when it can eat
and who it can love,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:47.166
I just don't think that's a far
stretch to owning people, okay?

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:49.468
I think about slavery a lot.

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:53.372
Because as I'm walking around,
minding my own business,

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:54.940
I am constantly told

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.876
that I look like different
civil-rights activists.

00:02:57.876 --> 00:02:59.211
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:00.813
And it needs to stop.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.082
That's rude that people
would say that to me.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.150
And I will take
a smattering of laughter

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.953
because what happens far too
often is a roomful of people

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:10.489
who just start shouting out
suggestions.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:14.360
Just "Sojourner Truth!
Ida B. Wells! Bessie Coleman!"

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.629
The one that I get the most,
the one that I've gotten

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:21.000
five times this year is that
I look like Harriet Tubman.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.436
-Woman: Aww.
-I will take -- Aww. Thank you.

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:27.607
I will take your, "Aww, no,"
because what's happened

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.576
far too often --
Recently, it was terrible.

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.079
A man just was like...

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.481
"Yes! Ohh!"

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.683
Like he had been sitting there
my whole set like,

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:40.186
"Mnh-mnh, mnh-mnh, mnh-mnh.
No.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.187
Why do I think of emancipation

00:03:42.187 --> 00:03:44.056
every time I look
at that woman?"

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.758
And I explained it to him,

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.626
and he felt seen
and I felt deeply hurt.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:50.396
It's frustrating
for a lot of reasons.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.965
One, because when people are
thinking of Harriet Tubman,

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:56.436
they're thinking
of an illustration.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:04:01.040
An illustration
of an 80-year-old woman.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.876
And it's like I know
I look tired, okay?

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.644
I know, I know.

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:08.480
But is this the type of
exhaustion that could only come

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.283
from picking cotton in a field?

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:13.519
Is that --
Is that what my face is giving?

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.421
And people are like,
"Come on, Kenice, no.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.823
It's the glasses.
It's the glasses."

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:21.527
And it's like,
"Oh, o-okay, it's...

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:25.598
it's just that Harriet Tubman
didn't wear glasses."

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.170
What would she need them for?

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.307
All that reading
she couldn't do?

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.675
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:38.277
-Kenice Mobley.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:41.247
For more info,
go to kenicemobley.com.

